cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this repository and the specific dated research entry or tool used.
  Preserve applicable license notices and credit the original sources as well.
type: software
title: "Noemesis: A Framework for Autonomous Mathematical Research"
url: "https://github.com/kbr-/math-research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kbr-/math-research"
authors:
  - family-names: Braun
    given-names: Kamil
abstract: >-
  An open, self-improving framework for autonomous mathematical research and
  on-demand formal verification, with persistent context, reproducible evidence,
  and a live, versioned notebook. Its first case study investigates superpolynomial
  ordinary pigeonhole-principle lower bounds in fixed-depth AC^0[p]-Frege. That
  goal remains open; working arguments and their limitations are explicitly recorded.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - proof complexity
  - pigeonhole principle
  - polynomial calculus
  - computational mathematics
